 "_about": "Crouched steps fire (T27, the owner 2026-10-23: crouch-walking still silent after #272; docs/notes/crouch_steps.md). A step sound is an animation event: the player subscribes on_player_sound_event (0x2A6470) to the clip channel player_sound_events, whose domain value 0 or 1 calls on_foot_step for one foot. Every standing run and sprint clip has that channel; the 16 moving crouch clips have only anim_intervals, so crouch-walking never called on_foot_step and the crouch pairs of crouch-steps-1.json never played. Each moving crouch clip gets the channel the way run, sprint and 0.31a2's crouch clips have it: two steps, 2 frames after each anim_intervals knot (2 and 17 of 30), with that interval's domain value (its foot). The bone tracks stay byte for byte. Live = stock 0.26g (no patch carries these clips).",
